## Project name: SAUSA-ERP

The user may say **SAUSA-ERP** to mean the whole product: VFP app repo (`E:\VFP\ERP_2`, GitHub `ERP_2-VFP`) **plus** SQL database/scripts (`SAUSA` DB, OneDrive `SQL` / GitHub `SQL-ERP_2`). Treat that name as code + data together unless they clearly mean only one side.

## Who runs SQL where

- **This Cursor session (home SuperMicro):** can run scripts against **local** SQL (`SuperMicro` / `SAUSA`). Do **not** assume connectivity or Windows auth to **BobWhite** (or other domain SQL) from here.
- **Domain PC (SAUSA):** Claude (or the user) runs create/deploy scripts against **BobWhite** (and optional `SA-WS-DK-26`).
- **OneDrive sync:** script/doc edits from either side land in `C:\Users\talkt\OneDrive - Space Alloys USA\SQL`. **Every time you work in that folder, re-read it** (status/diff/`SERVERS.md`/recent files) — do not trust an earlier session’s snapshot; watch for new commits, RUN-ORDER notes, and schema changes from the domain agent.

